{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Mr Brennan, in you go. Blood pressure outside was 138 over 84, and the pulse seventy two.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Grand, thanks. The bus was desperate, that's all.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (DOCTOR): You're grand, Sean. Sit down there. What's brought you in?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): It's the ear, doctor. This ringing. I can't get shut of it.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (DOCTOR): Tell me a bit more. Which ear, and how long?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): The right one. Umm, it was three weeks... no, a month. It's been a month. I don't know, doctor, I lose track.",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (DOCTOR): What sort of a sound is it?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): High. Uh, like a kettle whistling that never stops. Worse when the place is quiet, nights especially. Desperate.",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (DOCTOR): And your hearing, has that changed?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Muffled. Like cotton wool stuffed in the right ear. I don't know, doctor... actually no, I'm not imagining it, things are dull on that side.",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any pain, or discharge from the ear?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): No pain. No discharge. Nothing like that.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any dizziness or spinning?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Steady as anything.",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (DOCTOR): Headaches? Weakness anywhere?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): No. No headaches, no weakness. I'm fine apart from this. The allotment's drowned, mind you, with the rain.",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (DOCTOR): Ha, typical. What work are you at?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): Down the plant, the machinery. Fierce loud, I can't hear myself think in there. No ear protection either. I never wear the muffs.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (DOCTOR): How long in that job?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Fifteen years... sorry, sixteen. Sixteen years. I've overdone it with the noise, I know.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (DOCTOR): Ok. Any other health problems?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): Blood pressure. Had it a few years now. That's the only thing.",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (DOCTOR): On treatment for it?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): Rampiril. Ah ramipril, I mean. Two point five milligrams, no, five milligrams, every morning.",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (DOCTOR): Every morning without fail?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): Well, actually, I miss some. I don't know, doctor. A couple of times a week, maybe. I'm not great at it.",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (DOCTOR): Allergies to anything?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): No. None.",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (DOCTOR): And in the family, deafness or ear problems?",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): Dad went deaf when he got old. I don't know, doctor, if that's the same thing.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (DOCTOR): Different ages, often. I'll have a look in the ears.",
  "[SEG0032] person_3 (DOCTOR): Both canals are clear, no wax. The drums are intact. Right drum looks a shade dull, no redness.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (PATIENT): Mm. Is dull bad?",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (DOCTOR): Not on its own. I think this is noise-related tinnitus, and there may be hearing loss with that muffled feeling. That's provisional until the test.",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (PATIENT): Right. So what now?",
  "[SEG0036] person_3 (DOCTOR): I'm arranging a hearing test with audiology. That is booked, it'll be in the next couple of weeks.",
  "[SEG0037] person_3 (DOCTOR): We might do a scan if it does not settle. We won't do that now.",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): A scan. Ok. Do I see you again?",
  "[SEG0039] person_3 (DOCTOR): Let's see you in six weeks with the result. And wear ear muffs at work every shift, please. Give the ears a chance.",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (PATIENT): I'll do the muffs. The lads won't, but I will. Thanks, doctor.",
  "[SEG0041] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): I'll book that audiology on the system now, Mr Brennan. Letter will follow."
 ],
